    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0329" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg223"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Wright.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-20">September 20,
                            1906</date></hi>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 45, of the 11th ultimo, concerning the open door in Manchuria and
                    the importance of the establishment of customs-houses there.</p>
                <p>The department entertains the confident hope that the good disposition evidenced
                    by Japan will tend actively to the early adjustment of all these commercial
                    questions in Manchuria.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
